WEBVTT

00:00:00.577 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:07.510
In this lesson, we do a wispy set on a volume or mega volume base, step by step,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.589
and at the end,

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:09.870
how to do a wet look.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.590
Throughout the set, remember three things:

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:17.724
the client's eyes stay closed, each fan goes on exactly one natural lash,

00:00:17.674 --> 00:00:19.870
and glue never touches the skin.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:21.327
Step one:

00:00:21.582 --> 00:00:23.647
consultation and choosing the style.

00:00:23.985 --> 00:00:27.043
Show the client example photos, agree on how dramatic,

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.327
and how much the spikes should stand out.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:33.007
Explain the refill schedule, usually every two to three weeks.

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:35.647
Then look closely at the natural lashes.

00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:39.487
Strong, long, thick lashes get the full style.

00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:44.302
Fine, sparse lashes get the lighter version, and tell the client beforehand,

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:47.167
so she is not surprised when she opens her eyes.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:48.527
Step two:

00:00:48.773 --> 00:00:49.567
preparation.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:54.767
This is exactly the same as in the classic practice lesson and the lash preparation lesson:

00:00:55.108 --> 00:01:00.447
allergy questions, a comfortable position, cleansing, under eye pads, and brushing.

00:01:00.955 --> 00:01:03.807
If you have not seen them yet, watch those lessons first.

00:01:04.447 --> 00:01:05.333
Step three:

00:01:05.514 --> 00:01:06.373
draw the map.

00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:09.746
Divide the zones and write the lengths for the base layer,

00:01:09.696 --> 00:01:11.253
as in the lash mapping lesson.

00:01:11.678 --> 00:01:14.373
For wispy, also mark where the spikes go:

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:18.853
small dots on the pad, just under the lash line, evenly spaced.

00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:22.986
Spikes are usually one to three millimeters longer than the base layer,

00:01:22.936 --> 00:01:25.013
depending on the style the client chose.

00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:27.813
But never longer than the natural lash can carry.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.943
Before making fans, set up your station.

00:01:31.278 --> 00:01:35.743
A tray of very fine lashes for the base layer, arranged by the lengths on the map.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.383
A tray of longer lashes for the spikes.

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:41.023
A fresh drop of glue on the jade stone.

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:42.223
And your tweezers:

00:01:42.492 --> 00:01:46.383
a straight one for isolating, and volume tweezers for making fans.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.497
Keep everything neat, so your hands do not have to search,

00:01:49.447 --> 00:01:51.183
and you do not mix up the lengths.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:52.623
Step four:

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.943
make mega fans for the base layer.

00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:57.103
You make them as in the volume lesson:

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:02.303
pick up a few lashes, slide the tweezers, open the fan, then close the base.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.769
The only difference is more lashes, and finer ones,

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:07.823
so your hand has to be even lighter.

00:02:08.252 --> 00:02:13.503
The base of the fan must be small, closed, and almost as narrow as a single lash.

00:02:13.603 --> 00:02:18.223
Any fan with a wide base or a lopsided spread, throw it away and make another.

00:02:18.815 --> 00:02:19.665
Step five:

00:02:19.876 --> 00:02:20.705
take the glue.

00:02:21.132 --> 00:02:25.413
Touch only the base of the fan to the edge of the glue drop, very lightly,

00:02:25.363 --> 00:02:26.385
then pull it out.

00:02:26.803 --> 00:02:30.065
With mega volume, the amount of glue must be even smaller.

00:02:30.492 --> 00:02:35.105
If the base picks up a big blob of glue, throw that fan away and make a new one.

00:02:35.748 --> 00:02:36.626
Step six:

00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:38.066
the base layer first.

00:02:38.394 --> 00:02:43.642
Isolate a single natural lash, as in the classic lesson, then place the fan,

00:02:43.592 --> 00:02:47.266
with its base about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin.

00:02:48.004 --> 00:02:52.706
Alternate between the zones, as in the volume lesson, so the glue has time to cure.

00:02:53.119 --> 00:02:56.546
At each marked dot, leave a strong natural lash bare.

00:02:56.782 --> 00:03:01.426
That spot is saved for a spike, because each natural lash carries only one thing.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:05.026
When you finish, the base layer must be even and soft.

00:03:05.203 --> 00:03:05.986
No spikes yet.

00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:07.429
Step seven:

00:03:07.608 --> 00:03:08.629
make the spikes.

00:03:09.006 --> 00:03:12.549
Many brands sell ready made spikes, and they are fine to use.

00:03:12.985 --> 00:03:16.629
To make your own, pick up a few lashes, but do not open a fan:

00:03:16.978 --> 00:03:19.843
keep the lashes closed together into a single point,

00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:22.549
the way your trainer or your lash brand shows you.

00:03:22.973 --> 00:03:23.509
Check:

00:03:23.778 --> 00:03:26.869
the point must be straight and neat, with a small base.

00:03:27.218 --> 00:03:29.509
And still only a tiny bit of glue at the base.

00:03:30.161 --> 00:03:30.945
Step eight:

00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:33.345
place the spikes at the marked dots.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:36.618
Each spike goes on a single strong natural lash,

00:03:36.568 --> 00:03:39.025
in the same direction as the base layer.

00:03:39.364 --> 00:03:40.385
Space them evenly.

00:03:40.731 --> 00:03:45.445
Spikes bunched in one spot, or dense in some places and sparse in others,

00:03:45.395 --> 00:03:48.065
look messy, and lose the feathery effect.

00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:51.425
When one eye is done, look at the whole row again:

00:03:51.839 --> 00:03:53.425
is the rhythm of the spikes even?

00:03:54.093 --> 00:03:55.359
And what about wet look?

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.599
No open base layer is needed.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:02.643
The whole lash line uses closed fans, the lashes pressed together into points,

00:04:02.593 --> 00:04:04.399
each on its own natural lash,

00:04:04.511 --> 00:04:06.639
placed close together along the lash line.

00:04:07.148 --> 00:04:11.119
The points must be clearly separate, each point on its own natural lash.

00:04:11.395 --> 00:04:14.559
Several points stuck together are stickies, not a wet look.

00:04:14.902 --> 00:04:16.639
The glue still stays at the base.

00:04:16.796 --> 00:04:18.560
A closed point must stay soft,

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:22.559
never turning into a stiff stick because the glue crept up the lashes.

00:04:23.237 --> 00:04:24.092
Step nine:

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:24.732
check.

00:04:25.174 --> 00:04:29.052
Glide the straight tweezers lightly through the lashes, from base to tip:

00:04:29.328 --> 00:04:34.012
each fan, each spike, must stand alone on a single natural lash.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.732
If you see a sticky, separate it right away.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.052
Then look at the weight on each lash:

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.902
any natural lash that bends down or twists,

00:04:41.852 --> 00:04:44.812
remove the extension and replace it with a lighter,

00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:45.772
shorter fan.

00:04:46.187 --> 00:04:48.412
Look both from above and from the side.

00:04:48.668 --> 00:04:53.292
With lashes as full as mega volume, many stickies only show from the side.

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:54.737
Step ten:

00:04:54.995 --> 00:04:56.257
compare both eyes.

00:04:56.516 --> 00:05:00.017
Stand at the head of the bed, and look down at both eyes at once.

00:05:00.273 --> 00:05:04.900
The fullness, the length, and the spike positions must match on both sides,

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:05.937
as mirror images.

00:05:06.528 --> 00:05:07.388
Step eleven:

00:05:07.648 --> 00:05:08.348
finishing.

00:05:08.887 --> 00:05:10.230
Brush the lashes again,

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.108
remove the pads very gently while the client's eyes are still closed,

00:05:14.381 --> 00:05:16.188
then let her open her eyes slowly.

00:05:16.643 --> 00:05:19.068
Aftercare is as in the classic lesson:

00:05:19.258 --> 00:05:22.609
keep the lashes dry for as long as the glue maker advises,

00:05:22.559 --> 00:05:24.828
no oil based products at the lash base,

00:05:24.937 --> 00:05:26.988
brush them every day, no rubbing.

00:05:27.336 --> 00:05:30.028
With a dramatic style, add two more points.

00:05:30.188 --> 00:05:33.480
Full lashes easily collect dust and oil at the base,

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.348
so the client needs to wash her lashes gently,

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.907
with an oil free product, the way you show her.

00:05:39.248 --> 00:05:42.188
And book regular refills, and never leave it too long.

00:05:42.795 --> 00:05:44.264
Once the client has gone:

00:05:44.396 --> 00:05:47.929
used wands, swabs and pads go into a lidded bin,

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:50.903
and tweezers are cleaned and disinfected.

00:05:51.493 --> 00:05:55.304
Dramatic styles take a long time, and need a very light hand.

00:05:55.717 --> 00:05:57.464
Go slowly, and get it right.

00:05:57.947 --> 00:06:00.664
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
